## 8. Chat orchestrator

This is the heart of your application.

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ChatOrchestrator {

    private final IntentRouter intentRouter;
    private final RagService ragService;
    private final BusinessServiceDispatcher dispatcher;
    private final ResponseComposer responseComposer;

    public ChatResponseDto handle(ChatRequest request) {

        RouteDecision decision = intentRouter.route(request);

        if (decision.confidence() < 0.70) {
            return new ChatResponseDto(
                    request.conversationId(),
                    "I’m not fully sure which service should handle this. Can you clarify your request?"
            );
        }

        return switch (decision.target()) {
            case DOCUMENT_QA, GENERAL_QA -> {
                String answer = ragService.answer(request, decision);
                yield new ChatResponseDto(request.conversationId(), answer);
            }

            case ORDER_SERVICE,
                 CUSTOMER_SERVICE,
                 BILLING_SERVICE,
                 REPORT_GENERATION -> {
                ServiceResult serviceResult = dispatcher.dispatch(decision, request);
                String finalAnswer = responseComposer.compose(request, serviceResult);
                yield new ChatResponseDto(request.conversationId(), finalAnswer);
            }

            case HUMAN_HANDOFF -> new ChatResponseDto(
                    request.conversationId(),
                    "I’ll transfer this to a human agent."
            );

            case UNSUPPORTED -> new ChatResponseDto(
                    request.conversationId(),
                    "Sorry, I can’t help with that request yet."
            );
        };
    }
}
```

