## 10. RAG service with Spring AI

Simple RAG version:

```java
@Configuration
public class AiConfig {

    @Bean
    ChatClient ragChatClient(ChatModel chatModel, VectorStore vectorStore) {
        return ChatClient.builder(chatModel)
                .defaultSystem("""
                        You are a helpful assistant.
                        Answer using the retrieved context when available.
                        If the answer is not in the context, say you do not know.
                        Do not invent facts.
                        """)
                .defaultAdvisors(
                        QuestionAnswerAdvisor.builder(vectorStore).build()
                )
                .build();
    }
}
```

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class RagService {

    private final ChatClient ragChatClient;

    public String answer(ChatRequest request, RouteDecision decision) {
        return ragChatClient.prompt()
                .user(request.message())
                .call()
                .content();
    }
}
```

Spring AI provides `QuestionAnswerAdvisor` for the “naive RAG” pattern and also has `RetrievalAugmentationAdvisor` for more modular RAG flows. ([docs.spring.io](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/api/advisors.html?utm_source=openai))

For more advanced production RAG, prefer `RetrievalAugmentationAdvisor` when you need custom query transformation, metadata filtering, retrieval logic, or post-retrieval document processing.

