## 11. RAG with metadata filtering

You should store metadata with each document chunk:

```java
Map<String, Object> metadata = Map.of(
        "tenantId", tenantId,
        "sourceType", "PDF",
        "sourceId", fileId,
        "fileName", fileName,
        "userId", userId,
        "visibility", "PRIVATE"
);
```

Then retrieve only allowed documents.

Conceptually:

```java
String answer = chatClient.prompt()
        .user(request.message())
        .advisors(advisor -> advisor
                .param("filterExpression", "tenantId == '" + tenantId + "'"))
        .call()
        .content();
```

Use metadata filtering for:

```text
tenantId
userId
departmentId
documentType
securityLevel
sourceSystem
createdAt
language
```

This is essential. Without metadata filtering, one user may retrieve another user’s document chunks.

