## 13. CSV ingestion

CSV usually needs custom logic because rows have structure. Do not simply embed the raw CSV file as one large text block.

Example approach:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class CsvIngestionService {

    private final VectorStore vectorStore;

    public void ingestCsv(InputStream inputStream, String tenantId, String sourceId) throws IOException {

        Reader reader = new InputStreamReader(inputStream);

        CSVParser parser = CSVFormat.DEFAULT
                .builder()
                .setHeader()
                .setSkipHeaderRecord(true)
                .build()
                .parse(reader);

        List<Document> docs = new ArrayList<>();

        for (CSVRecord record : parser) {
            String text = record.toMap().entrySet().stream()
                    .map(e -> e.getKey() + ": " + e.getValue())
                    .collect(Collectors.joining("\n"));

            Map<String, Object> metadata = Map.of(
                    "tenantId", tenantId,
                    "sourceId", sourceId,
                    "sourceType", "CSV",
                    "rowNumber", record.getRecordNumber()
            );

            docs.add(new Document(text, metadata));
        }

        TokenTextSplitter splitter = new TokenTextSplitter();
        vectorStore.add(splitter.apply(docs));
    }
}
```

Recommended CSV strategies:

| CSV type | Strategy |
|---|---|
| Small FAQ CSV | One row = one document |
| Product catalog | One product = one document |
| Transactions | Usually do **not** embed all rows; query database directly |
| Analytics/reporting CSV | Store structured data in DB, use tools/SQL, not only RAG |

