## 15. Ingesting responses from other services

If another service returns JSON, normalize it into documents.

Example:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ServiceResponseIngestionService {

    private final VectorStore vectorStore;
    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper;

    public void ingestServiceResponse(
            String json,
            String tenantId,
            String sourceSystem,
            String entityId
    ) throws JsonProcessingException {

        JsonNode root = objectMapper.readTree(json);

        String text = flattenJson(root);

        Document document = new Document(
                text,
                Map.of(
                        "tenantId", tenantId,
                        "sourceType", "SERVICE_RESPONSE",
                        "sourceSystem", sourceSystem,
                        "entityId", entityId
                )
        );

        vectorStore.add(List.of(document));
    }

    private String flattenJson(JsonNode node) {
        // Implement your own JSON-to-readable-text logic.
        return node.toPrettyString();
    }
}
```

But be careful: if the data is highly structured and frequently updated — orders, invoices, balances, inventory — prefer **tool calling / service calls** over RAG. RAG is better for knowledge retrieval; APIs/databases are better for live transactional data.

