## 16. Service routing and tool execution

You can implement routing manually:

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class BusinessServiceDispatcher {

    private final OrderService orderService;
    private final BillingService billingService;
    private final CustomerService customerService;
    private final ReportService reportService;

    public ServiceResult dispatch(RouteDecision decision, ChatRequest request) {
        return switch (decision.target()) {
            case ORDER_SERVICE -> orderService.handle(request);
            case BILLING_SERVICE -> billingService.handle(request);
            case CUSTOMER_SERVICE -> customerService.handle(request);
            case REPORT_GENERATION -> reportService.handle(request);
            default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unsupported route: " + decision.target());
        };
    }
}
```

Or expose methods as Spring AI tools. Spring AI’s tool calling support lets a model interact with APIs/tools, and Spring AI’s `ChatClient` can run tool-calling loops through its advisor chain. ([docs.spring.io](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/api/tools.html?utm_source=openai))

Example tool:

```java
@Component
public class OrderTools {

    private final OrderService orderService;

    public OrderTools(OrderService orderService) {
        this.orderService = orderService;
    }

    @Tool(description = "Get order status by order id")
    public OrderStatus getOrderStatus(String orderId) {
        return orderService.getOrderStatus(orderId);
    }
}
```

Then configure:

```java
@Bean
ChatClient toolEnabledChatClient(ChatModel chatModel, OrderTools orderTools) {
    return ChatClient.builder(chatModel)
            .defaultTools(orderTools)
            .defaultSystem("""
                    You are a business assistant.
                    Use tools when the user asks about live business data.
                    Use RAG when the user asks about documentation or policy.
                    """)
            .build();
}
```

My recommendation: for critical business actions, use **manual dispatch** first. Use autonomous tool calling only after you have strong logging, validation, approval workflows, and tests.

