## 17. Response composer

After a service responds, let the LLM produce a user-friendly answer.

```java
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ResponseComposer {

    private final ChatClient chatClient;

    public String compose(ChatRequest request, ServiceResult result) {
        return chatClient.prompt()
                .system("""
                        You convert internal service results into clear user-facing answers.
                        Do not expose internal IDs, stack traces, implementation details, or secrets.
                        If the service result contains an error, explain it safely.
                        """)
                .user("""
                        User question:
                        %s

                        Service result:
                        %s
                        """.formatted(request.message(), result))
                .call()
                .content();
    }
}
```

