## 27. My recommended architecture for your project

Use this:

```text
Spring Boot monolith first, modularized internally:

com.yourcompany.chat
  ├── api
  ├── orchestration
  ├── routing
  ├── rag
  ├── ingestion
  ├── tools
  ├── services
  ├── security
  ├── observability
  └── persistence
```

Start with PGVector unless you already have a dedicated vector DB requirement. Use Spring AI RAG advisors for document Q&A. Use manual dispatch for business services. Add tool calling later when your guardrails are mature.

This gives you a clean, production-oriented chatbot that can handle PDFs, CSVs, images, service responses, RAG, and routing without turning the whole system into an unpredictable “LLM decides everything” agent.
